Z||000000||Lewis||03-03-2001||05:28 PM||||I currently own a 85gt with auto trans.  I seen a 88 coupe today and took it for a test drive.  There is nothing fancy about this car..only extra on this car is power mirrors and sunroof..no air..interior will need work..the body is in fine shape but only has 4cyl with auto.  Needs work on motor problably valve cover gasket.  Only has 119,000 km.  He is asking 3000 canadian..I am thinking of buying this car and make some improvements..mainly putting my six in it..my question is ...is the car worth the price and worth the work to put my six out of the gt into the 88..any suggestions would help...thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-03-2001||05:48 PM||||I think it is a great Idea, but I am a little biased toward 88's. The engine swap was easy except for the fuel pump.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||03-03-2001||11:10 PM||||The biggest advantage to the 88 is the suspension. And you won't notice it on a casual drive. Personally, I love the 88s. I am turning an 88 coupe of mine into a customized hot rod Indy clone. <P>If you get it, good luck.. and have fun!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||03-05-2001||08:44 AM||||I think the '88 brakes make an even bigger difference than the suspension - the pedal is rock hard and they don't fade.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Will||03-05-2001||10:41 AM||||3000 Canadian... What's that--$650 American?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   I say go for it but see if you can talk him down on price, obviously.<P>Do you like automatics? I would say that when you do the engine swap would be the perfect time for an auto to stick conversion.||||reg||1
